-- The amount: "security for the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount that the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the
-- adjudication determination or judgment".  The text says the security is for the unpaid portion, so the portion is the adjudicated
-- amount less what the applicant has already paid (never below nothing); for example 100,000 adjudicated less 40,000 paid is 60,000.
-- src:5263 | (2) The applicant must, at the time of filing the application, provide security for the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount that the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment by means of a direction to the Accountant ‑ General in Form 44.
@ref O 36 r 3(2) (src:5263-5263)
GIVEN `the adjudicated amount the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that amount the applicant has already paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` MEANS
    IF `the part of that amount the applicant has already paid` AT LEAST `the adjudicated amount the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the adjudicated amount the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment` MINUS `the part of that amount the applicant has already paid`

-- src:5263 | (2) The applicant must, at the time of filing the application, provide security for the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount that the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment by means of a direction to the Accountant ‑ General in Form 44.
@ref O 36 r 3(2) (src:5263-5263)
GIVEN `the adjudicated amount the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of that amount the applicant has already paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the security provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 36 r 3(2) the security provided is for the unpaid portion` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the security provided` EQUALS `o 36 r 3(2) the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount` `the adjudicated amount the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment` `the part of that amount the applicant has already paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must ... provide security for the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount"; the text does not say what follows security of another amount (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)

-- "At the time of filing the application": the date of the direction is the date of the filing (ruling: a time stated as
-- "at the time of" is read as the same date; a different date answers JUST FALSE).
-- src:5263 | (2) The applicant must, at the time of filing the application, provide security for the unpaid portion of the adjudicated amount that the applicant is required to pay in consequence of the adjudication determination or judgment by means of a direction to the Accountant ‑ General in Form 44.
@ref O 36 r 3(2) (src:5263-5263)
GIVEN `the date the security was provided` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 36 r 3(2) the security is provided at the time of filing` MEANS
    IF `the date the security was provided` EQUALS `the date the application was filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of filing the application"

-- src:5264 | (3) If the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application referred to in paragraph (1), the party must file an affidavit stating the grounds on which the party opposes the application within 14 days after being served with the application and the supporting affidavit.
@ref O 36 r 3(3) the period (src:5264-5264)
`o 36 r 3(3) the period for the party entitled to enforce to file an opposing affidavit` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:5264 | (3) If the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application referred to in paragraph (1), the party must file an affidavit stating the grounds on which the party opposes the application within 14 days after being served with the application and the supporting affidavit.
@ref O 36 r 3(3) (src:5264-5264)
GIVEN `the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application arises` MEANS
    IF `the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application"

