        IF `the affidavit states the grounds on which the party opposes the application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "stating the grounds"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)

-- src:5265 | (4) In this Rule, “judgment” means a judgment obtained pursuant to section 27.
