    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“judgment” means a judgment obtained pursuant to section 27"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 36 -- the same duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names no consequence of a late act, so a late act is a BREACH only in the sense that the period has run
-- (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do).  Days are a plain count; the count the Rules require
-- is O 3 r 3 (see the decision functions).

DECLARE `o 36 party under Order 36` IS ONE OF
    `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor`
    `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor`
    `o 36 r 3(3) the party entitled to enforce`

DECLARE `o 36 act under Order 36` IS ONE OF
    `o 36 r 2(4) apply to set aside the adjudication determination`
    `o 36 r 2(4) enforce the adjudication determination`
    `o 36 r 3(3) file the affidavit opposing the application`

-- The debtor's permission: a MAY.  On this build a MAY that lapses unused is FULFILLED, so no trace can show the
-- window closing; the decision function above does.
-- src:5252 | (4) Within 14 days after being served with the order granting permission, the debtor may apply to set aside the adjudication determination and the adjudication determination must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the adjudication determination, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 36 r 2(4) (src:5252-5252)
`o 36 r 2(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the adjudication determination` MEANS
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the debtor`
    MAY `o 36 r 2(4) apply to set aside the adjudication determination`
    WITHIN (`o 36 r 2(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the adjudication determination`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The bar on enforcing: a SHANT.  Enforcing inside the period is the violation.
-- src:5252 | (4) Within 14 days after being served with the order granting permission, the debtor may apply to set aside the adjudication determination and the adjudication determination must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the adjudication determination, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 36 r 2(4) (src:5252-5252)
`o 36 r 2(4) the bar on enforcing the adjudication determination` MEANS
    PARTY `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor`
    SHANT `o 36 r 2(4) enforce the adjudication determination`
    WITHIN (`o 36 r 2(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the adjudication determination`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 36 r 2(4) the creditor` BECAUSE "the adjudication determination was enforced before the expiration of the period for the debtor to apply to set it aside"

-- src:5264 | (3) If the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application referred to in paragraph (1), the party must file an affidavit stating the grounds on which the party opposes the application within 14 days after being served with the application and the supporting affidavit.
@ref O 36 r 3(3) (src:5264-5264)
GIVEN `the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN
`o 36 r 3(3) the duty to file an affidavit opposing the application` MEANS
    IF `the party who is entitled to enforce the adjudication determination or the judgment wishes to oppose the application`
    THEN PARTY `o 36 r 3(3) the party entitled to enforce`
         MUST `o 36 r 3(3) file the affidavit opposing the application`
         WITHIN (`o 36 r 3(3) the period for the party entitled to enforce to file an opposing affidavit`'s `period length`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `o 36 r 3(3) the party entitled to enforce` BECAUSE "the affidavit was not filed within 14 days after service of the application and the supporting affidavit"
    ELSE FULFILLED
